 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [Position-Normal Tree](4222-position-normal-tree.md)
-A binary tree hierarchy over a triangle mesh where leaves are triangles and internal nodes store an axis-aligned bounding box (AABB) for positions and a bounding cone for shading normals [4222-position-normal-tree.md]. It enables hierarchical pruning of refractive path searches by eliminating subtrees that cannot contain valid refraction points, addressing the performance bottleneck of testing all triangles in large meshes [4222-position-normal-tree.md]. It is distinguished from interval-based refinement by prioritizing speed over guaranteed convergence, typically running 2 to 5 times faster while producing visually equivalent results [4222-position-normal-tree.md].
+A binary tree hierarchy over a triangle mesh where leaves are triangles and internal nodes contain a 3D axis-aligned bounding box (AABB) over positions and a bounding cone over shading normals for all descendants. It stores position and normal information for boundary triangles to enable hierarchical pruning of refractive path searches. It is distinguished from interval-based refinement by prioritizing speed over guaranteed convergence, typically running 2 to 5 times faster while producing visually equivalent results.
 
 ### [Voxel Mesh Ray Intersection via BVH](6900-voxel-mesh-ray-intersection-via-bvh.md)
-Voxel Mesh Ray Intersection via BVH is a raycasting method for voxel meshes that traverses a grid of oriented sub-cubes to find intersections with voxel geometry using Binary Volume Hierarchy (BVH) triangle intersection tests [6900-voxel-mesh-ray-intersection-via-bvh.md, unofficial]. It handles multiple meshes by first checking bounding boxes and then delegating to the specific mesh's BVH [6900-voxel-mesh-ray-intersection-via-bvh.md, unofficial]. This method builds on [Mesh BVH](1062-mesh-bvh.md) by providing the specific traversal logic and data structures required to query triangle meshes stored within a voxelized world structure [6900-voxel-mesh-ray-intersection-via-bvh.md, unofficial].
